      "content": "The DEP-2026 specs detail a shift to distributed ledger technology for energy transaction validation, focusing on peer-to-peer energy routing. Shifting to the local hardware switch model will inherently increase localized response times, which could initially introduce minor fluctuations in frequency stability margins. However, the inherent redundancy of the decentralized architecture offers superior resilience against single points of failure, potentially improving overall long-term stability under stress.",
      "source": "target",
